      "location": "/sections/1/blocks/0/text",
      "text": "A London ordinary-share quote in GBp must first be divided by 100 to obtain GBP. Converting a dated GBP share value to euro requires an explicitly dated EUR-per-GBP spot. For example, the controlled test uses 4,500 GBp and 1.20 EUR per GBP to obtain EUR54; neither number is a market observation or forecast. The delivered input cells are blank and show MISSING. Price-specific value/return conclusions are withheld.",
